= Semantic Web — Simple =

The '''Semantic Web''' is an approach for putting structured, linked data on the Web so computers can understand more of the relationships between things.

Instead of only linking one webpage to another, Semantic Web data can say:

<pre>
Mars → is a → Planet
Mars → orbits → Sun
</pre>

Important technologies include:
* [[Resource Description Framework/Simple|RDF]];
* [[Web Ontology Language/Simple|OWL]];
* SPARQL;
* SKOS.

These standards give data shared identifiers and defined relationships.

The Semantic Web does not mean computers understand everything like humans.

It means more of the meaning is written explicitly in a form software can process.

